  "description": "The University of Tokyo is a national research university in Tokyo, founded in 1877 as Japan's first modern university. It has ten faculties and its main campuses are at Hongo and Komaba.",
  "whyIncluded": "The Public Service Commission places scholars at the University of Tokyo, its medical degree is on the Singapore Medical Council's list of registrable basic medical qualifications, and Japan is among the ten destinations with the most Singaporean students abroad (about 270 in UNESCO UIS data for 2022-24).",
  "livingCosts": {
    "year": 2026,
    "months": 12,
    "monthly": {
      "housing": 90000,
      "food": 55000,
      "transport": 6000,
      "personal": 20000
    },
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.u-tokyo.ac.jp/adm/inbound/en/finance-living.html",
    "lastVerified": "2026-09-23",
    "sourceType": "official",
    "notes": "UTokyo 'Living Expenses' page gives only rent and food: a one-room apartment typically ¥80,000-¥100,000/month (midpoint used; rent only, utilities not included) and food ¥50,000-¥60,000/month (midpoint). Transport and personal are not given by UTokyo, so they are JASSO 2023 Lifestyle Survey of Privately-Financed International Students (table 7-4) Tokyo averages: commuting ¥6,000; personal = hobbies/leisure ¥10,000 + other daily costs ¥10,000 (https://www.studyinjapan.go.jp/ja/_mt/2026/09/re_Seikatsu2023zittai.pdf)."
